**Executable gate contract.** The compiled sibling gate snapshot is the resolved membership, prerequisites and selection contract. Check acceptance coverage against the immutable oracle; do not expand the roster from generic applicability rules.

**Authorized effects.** {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/EmbeddedChartTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/CategoryEditorWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SampleEditorWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}

**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryEditorWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleEditorWindowTests`

**How to implement.** The UI suite's material, category and sample-editor facts read the shipped catalogue instead of the code seeds (001 §B 'tests load the same files'; the S1.7 brief: re-point every test that reads a seed value to the BuiltinCatalogue fixture, numbers unchanged). Files, all in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/`: `MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs`, `MaterialsWindowTests.fs`, `EmbeddedChartTests.fs`, `NkDispersionChartTests.fs`, `CategoryEditorWindowTests.fs`, `SampleEditorWindowTests.fs`. Re-point rules (S1.7; the same in every re-point step). `builtInEntries` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`; `standardCategories` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()`; `MaterialLibrary.standard` (written `standard` under `open MaterialLibrary`) becomes `{ entries = BuiltinCatalogue.materials () }`; `SeedSamples.allSeedSamples` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()`; `SeedSamples.<name>` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.<name>Id` and `SeedSamples.<name>.id` becomes `SampleIds.<name>Id` (step 15's names); `SeedSources.allSeedSources` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sources ()`; `SeedSources.reference600` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.source600`; the `SeedSources.tunables` list becomes `[ PresetIds.xenonMonochromator; PresetIds.tiSapphireTunable; PresetIds.supercontinuum; PresetIds.euvBeamline ] |> List.map BuiltinCatalogue.source`, and one tunable source becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.xenonMonochromator`; `seedEntries` becomes `(BuiltinCatalogue.samples () |> List.map SampleItem) @ BuiltinCatalogue.presets ()`; `Library.createInMemory ()` (written `createInMemory ()` under `open Library`) becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`; and the self-seeding stores become the fixture's doubles with the same arguments (step 45): `MaterialProxy.createInMemory r v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore r v`, `SampleProxy.createInMemory v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore v` and `CategoryProxy.createInMemory r` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categoryStore r`. A fact that took a seed by its list position (`List.head`, `List.item`) takes the same entry by its well-known id (`MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds`, `SampleIds`, `PresetIds`), so it still tests the entry it tested; a fact that compared ordered lists built from the seed lists builds both sides from the fixture, and compares order-independently only where the product's order is not the fixture's row order (the S1.3 step 20 precedent). Every fact keeps its name and its assertions, every count and every number stays. A comment or doc, an `open`'s trailing comment included, that names a seed or a self-seeding store names the fixture member instead, in no more words, and an `open` nothing needs any more goes. No product file, fixture member or fact is added. Per file: `MaterialEditorWindowTests`' `builtIn` helper reads `BuiltinCatalogue.material`; `SampleEditorWindowTests`' stub material proxy answers from `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`, and every `initSampleEditor context builtInEntries` passes `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`; `CategoryEditorWindowTests`' stub proxy starts from `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()` and counts against it; the stores of `MaterialsWindowTests`, `EmbeddedChartTests` and `NkDispersionChartTests` come from the doubles.

**Acceptance.** After the re-point, `git grep -n -E "SeedSamples|SeedSources|seedEntries|seedTrees|builtInEntries|standardCategories|seedExperiments|(MaterialProxy|SampleProxy|CategoryProxy).createInMemory |Library.createInMemory " -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/EmbeddedChartTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/CategoryEditorWindowTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SampleEditorWindowTests.fs MUST find nothing; ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the touched classes with their counts unchanged; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.
